From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the digital internal mic at the first sign-in too

Chrome 0091 made the digital internal mic (AMD ACP, Intel SOF DMIC) win a
tie in LessBuiltInPriority. On the AMD test PC (23u, its saved audio choices
cleared) Chrome still chose the HD-Audio codec's unwired "Internal Mic":
when a device set is new and nothing was active before, CrasAudioHandler::
HandleSystemBoots activates the first internal device CRAS lists, without
comparing them, and the codec's comes first.

There, the internal device LessBuiltInPriority ranks first is activated.

diff --git a/chromeos/ash/components/audio/cras_audio_handler.cc b/chromeos/ash/components/audio/cras_audio_handler.cc
index 3175bcee90678..6db56196a920d 100644
--- a/chromeos/ash/components/audio/cras_audio_handler.cc
+++ b/chromeos/ash/components/audio/cras_audio_handler.cc
@@ -2310,15 +2310,24 @@ void CrasAudioHandler::HandleSystemBoots(bool is_input,
 
   // Otherwise when no most recent activated device, if there is an internal
   // device, activate it and show notification.
+  // NickelOS: of several, the one LessBuiltInPriority ranks first, not the
+  // first CRAS lists: a laptop with a digital mic often has the HD-Audio
+  // codec's unwired internal mic listed before it (Chrome 0091; the AMD test PC
+  // still recorded silence on 23u, chosen here at the first sign-in).
+  const AudioDevice* internal_device = nullptr;
   for (const AudioDevice& device : devices) {
-    if (device.type == AudioDeviceType::kInternalSpeaker ||
-        device.type == AudioDeviceType::kInternalMic) {
-      SwitchToDevice(device, /*notify=*/true,
-                     DeviceActivateType::kActivateByPriority);
-      should_show_notification_ = true;
-      return;
+    if ((device.type == AudioDeviceType::kInternalSpeaker ||
+         device.type == AudioDeviceType::kInternalMic) &&
+        (!internal_device || LessBuiltInPriority(*internal_device, device))) {
+      internal_device = &device;
     }
   }
+  if (internal_device) {
+    SwitchToDevice(*internal_device, /*notify=*/true,
+                   DeviceActivateType::kActivateByPriority);
+    should_show_notification_ = true;
+    return;
+  }
 
   // Otherwise when no most recent activated device and no internal device (a
   // brand new chromebox), activate the highest priority and show
